{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1535582-alternate-otherworlds-structure","id":1535582,"title":"Alternate Otherworlds Structure","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-05-14T13:03:06-07:00","id":1535582,"title":"Alternate Otherworlds Structure","content":"This is something I've been pondering recently. If we could toss out the existing structure of the otherworlds and remake it from scratch, without having to worry too much about other game lines, how would you do it?<br /> <br /> For my own part I'd probably:<br /> <br /> - Move away from a clearly defined gauntlet. <br /> - Make the astral, spirit, and under worlds very different things and not just different flavors of umbra. <br /> - Move more of the strangeness into the physical world.<br /> - Make more room for realms that don't actually fit anywhere but exist anyways<br /> <br /> I haven't gotten much further than that. What would you do?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-14T13:20:31-07:00","id":1535587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1535582-alternate-otherworlds-structure#post1535582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Make the astral, spirit, and under worlds very different things and not just different flavors of umbra.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this would not work. Look at the dreaming, its a mess no one wants to touch.<br /> <br /> My personal idea is that the otherworlds (can be called umbras why not) are the connected worlds of demon the fallen before there was just one after the fall.<br /> So every world is connected. Some things exist in many worlds. Whats a fire in the material plane could be a elemental in the spirit world, and could be a relic in the underworld and could be a commet in the horrizontal realm. Ofcourse things that that translate to multiple worlds would be rare.<br /> <br /> As a Lovecraft fan i would build those worlds as layers around the Abyss. Where in the abyss there are cthulhu monsters. Guarded by another monster that is reality itself in the form of omnipotent light. I dont mind keeping the 3 umbras as its hard as it is to imagine them sometimes but would keep them far less defined.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-14T14:58:05-07:00","id":1535590,"title":"","content":"To me the greater problem is that they can't decide if Umbra is a place, a common name to several places, or a medium to reach places.<br /> <br /> I think <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar758_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"758\" data-vbnamecard=\"758\">Ramnesis</a> general idea is good, but I would throw away the very name &quot;Umbra&quot; and instead call those realities just &quot;Realms&quot;, with &quot;Astral&quot; and &quot;Spirit&quot; being classifications for realms.<br /> <br /> Also, specify the three &quot;Penumbrae&quot; as distinct mirror-realms, either with clear, practical means of interaction, or no interaction whatsoever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-14T15:33:06-07:00","id":1535593,"title":"","content":"I think the place to start with what you want is to look at the word &quot;umbra&quot; itself. Umbra means shadow. <br /> <br /> Try this, if the Astral, Spirit, Dream, and underworld, are all shadows (umbras), what are they shadows of?<br /> <br /> Is physical reality itself an Umbra? <br /> <br /> If all these realities are shadows of something, what is the illumination that allows the shadows to be cast? <br /> <br /> Answering these questions in your game makes organizing reality easier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-14T21:37:03-07:00","id":1535609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1535582-alternate-otherworlds-structure#post1535582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is something I've been pondering recently. If we could toss out the existing structure of the otherworlds and remake it from scratch, without having to worry too much about other game lines, how would you do it?<br /> <br /> For my own part I'd probably:<br /> <br /> - Move away from a clearly defined gauntlet.<br /> - Make the astral, spirit, and under worlds very different things and not just different flavors of umbra.<br /> - Move more of the strangeness into the physical world.<br /> - Make more room for realms that don't actually fit anywhere but exist anyways<br /> <br /> I haven't gotten much further than that. What would you do?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm doing this exactly thing, although I'm never satisfied with the results. I'm creating a new spirit world from scratch.<br /> <br /> I do however have a VERY interesting framework that I decided to adopt.<br /> <br /> I'm basing it in the HUMAN MIND.<br /> <br /> I saw a few lectures about Gnosticism/Hermeticism (I won't get in details), and I liked the idea of &quot;As Above, so Bellow&quot;.<br /> <br /> Thus, I decided to structure the &quot;world&quot; based on the structure of the human mind. &quot;As Above, so Bellow&quot;, Gnosticism and Hermeticism upholds a very Kantian idea that the universe is &quot;immaterial&quot;. Sure, for Kant, in a very resumed and somewhat cartoonish way (but not untrue), we are just &quot;minds floating in the Ether&quot; and &quot;reality&quot; is just a &quot;matrix created by God&quot;. To Gnosticism/Hermeticism, we are all &quot;Shards of the Divine&quot;, aka our &quot;souls&quot;, each one of them, are &quot;fragments of God&quot;... And this &quot;reality&quot; is just a mental &quot;illusion&quot; constructed by God, but &quot;God&quot; forgot that he is God, because WE ARE GOD, each one of us, and we must remember that fact and reunite as One (does that ring a bell? Celestial Choristers? The One?).<br /> <br /> Anyway. I find that to be utter lunacy, but I liked this idea. So I decided that it would be awesome to structure the spirit world in the same way as our mind.<br /> <br /> And so I did. And I gotta say, the results truly amazed me. I used Freudian and Jungian concepts of psychology to structure my first draft; for instance, the &quot;Astral Plane&quot; I made it to be analogous to our &quot;Pre Conscious Mind&quot;, the Jungian idea about those thoughts that, while not immediately surfacing, are easily and readily available at any time.<br /> <br /> So, for instance, you may not be thinking about your sister's marriage 10 years ago at this moment, but if I ask you about it, you can immediately recollect it from memory. That's our Pre Conscious Mind.<br /> <br /> So, as the &quot;Astral Plane&quot;, this turned into a plane of pure Thought that connects the entire Spiritual World. Yes, the Astral Plane is accessible with Mind 4. But I defined that you CAN'T enter other realms from it using Mind alone; it always displeased me such a possibility.<br /> <br /> But wait; the Astral Plane is like a &quot;membrane&quot; that connects all other planes; and yes, this is to mimic our &quot;Pre Conscious Mind&quot;. Some thoughts we can access when we wish... But some others are buried deep in our subconscious. Also, there are &quot;intrusive thoughts&quot;... Those instances when we think about really dark stuff completely out of the blue (&quot;I wish I could murder my boss&quot; or &quot;how would it be to date my cousin&quot;).<br /> <br /> So, there's a &quot;navigation system&quot; inside the Astral Plane. And, if you fail... You may end up in HELL.<br /> <br /> Yes, I designed &quot;Hell&quot; as a plane. I also designed &quot;The Abyss&quot; and the &quot;Shadowlands&quot;.<br /> <br /> Hell is the &quot;disharmony&quot; between Ego, Id and Superego. And I designed it divided into 7 &quot;subplanes&quot; if I'm not mistaken, now I don't quite remember. One &quot;Hell&quot; for the Ego, one &quot;Hell&quot; for the Id, one for the Superego, 3 for the disharmony between each of them, and one &quot;Hell&quot; which is actually &quot;Integration&quot;, so this &quot;Hell&quot; is actually for those that went through the necessary crucible of that realm and emerged anew from the experience. It's a &quot;piece of Paradise in Hell&quot; sort of thing.<br /> <br /> Now, if you're Navigating over the Astral Plane and you &quot;get lost&quot;, you may end up in the &quot;gates of hell&quot;... That's akin to when we are lost in thoughts and our mind drift towards intrusive dark thoughts. The Astral Plane is &quot;more mental than spiritual&quot; however, and there's a kind of &quot;Gauntlet&quot; between each realm. So, if you end up at the &quot;Gates of Hell&quot;, you'll see a mirrored image of each, reflected in the &quot;membrane&quot;. That membrane is like our intrusive thoughts; but it's not the same as diving deeply into the depravity of our most animalistic and primitive instincts; we quickly shut off those thoughts, but they exist somewhere inside of our minds.<br /> <br /> &quot;Demons&quot; are, therefore, likewise out intrusive thoughts running amok. When a &quot;demon&quot; escapes from hell, is like when we let one intrusive thought take hold. &quot;I wanna kill myself&quot;. If we don't shut off that kind of thought, it will quickly degenerate our mental health. Thus, such is the nature of &quot;demons&quot;.<br /> <br /> I've made several other planes. The &quot;Shadowlands&quot; is an aspect of the Jungian concept of the Shadow, our darker self, but one crucial part of our psyche. No, not were ghosts dwell. Ghosts come from the &quot;Underworld&quot;, and that's part of our memory.<br /> <br /> The Dreamlands are pretty self explanatory, and part of my &quot;Middle Umbra&quot;. The Middle Umbra is related to our Subconscious.<br /> <br /> Then we have the &quot;Upper Umbra&quot; or &quot;High Umbra&quot;, which holds the Realms related to the ARCHETYPES, the Jungian Concept of Archetypes. The lower level of it is the &quot;Personal Archetypes&quot;, and the higher level is the &quot;Collective Unconscious&quot;. With Realms representing the Shadow that I already mentioned, but also several other Archetypes, with my favorites being the &quot;Wise King&quot; vs &quot;The Tyrant&quot;, the &quot;Holy Mother&quot; (like Virgin Mary) and the &quot;Dark Mother&quot; (like the Hindu goddess Kali, but also Lilith and others). I love those, they represent at the end of the day the good vs the bad parents. The Wise King is the good father, the man that guides his children towards achievement in life, like the King Solomon from the Bible, while The Tyrant is the bad father who destroys his children, best represented by the Greek Titan Chronus devouring his own children. The same with the Holy/Dark Mother figures, with the Holy Mother being the nurturing figure of life, like Virgin Mary, and the Dark Mother like Kali devouring her own offspring.<br /> <br /> But that's not all. The Material Plane, in this representation, represents THE BODY. It is, therefore, &quot;outside of the mind&quot;.<br /> <br /> And then, there is the &quot;Qlipphotic Umbra&quot; that which exists BEYOND, the place from where the Nefandi and Things-Men-Were-Not-Meant-To-Know come from.<br /> <br /> And that's a representation of the EXTERIOR WORLD. Everything that isn't inside of the human mind is, therefore, alien, and part of the Qlipphotic Umbra, the anti-life anti-existance non-realm beyond.<br /> <br /> And much, much more. The &quot;Penumbra&quot; (I didn't call it that, but let's roll with it) is a representation of our SENSES. Thus, it is a representation of what we see, hear, smell and so on. I called it &quot;Mirror Realm&quot;, because it has several &quot;mirrors&quot; connecting it to other Realms - usually connecting it to the Astral Plane, because, the senses induce your Pre Conscious Mind, but sometimes it can lead to other planes.<br /> <br /> And so <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28035,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","user":"Magus Maximus","date":". 05-15-2024, 01:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-14T22:20:26-07:00","id":1535612,"title":"","content":"But that was just my first draft, of which I will still take some parts - oh yes, I also created a &quot;Heaven&quot;, being representations of healthy Ego, Superego and Id.<br /> <br /> I had also assigned &quot;rulers&quot; to each one of them. For instance, each of the 3 &quot;realms of Heaven&quot; where ruled by God, Holy Spirit and Jesus in conjunction with Bhrama, Vishnu and Shiva, each one of them representing either Ego, Superego or I'd.<br /> <br /> Then I assigned mythological figures to be the &quot;rulers&quot; of each realm, like Apolo, Odin, Ra and so on.<br /> <br /> But now I'm starting all over again, because I decided to make a change.<br /> <br /> You see, my first draft was only from a psychological point of view.<br /> <br /> Now, I decided to include a &quot;neurological Umbra&quot;.<br /> <br /> What I mean with that is that I want another spiritual plane that is connected to both our neurology and our psyche.<br /> <br /> Thus, I created 2 main &quot;Umbras&quot;, one which is more &quot;ethereal&quot; because it is connected to human thoughts, while the other is more &quot;visceral&quot;, because it is connected to the physiology of our nervous system.<br /> <br /> Funnily enough, this landed itself well with the WoD idea that Werewolves and Mages deal in &quot;different places of the Umbra&quot;. Thus, the were-beasts are more attuned to the &quot;physiological Umbra&quot; while Mages are more attuned towards the &quot;psychological Umbra&quot;.<br /> <br /> So, for example, &quot;Axis Mundi&quot;, which means &quot;Center of the World&quot;, a mystical concept present in many mythologies that talk about a high mountain (Mount Olympus) or the &quot;Three of Life&quot; (like the Norse Yggdrasil), is a Realm that represents the Spinal Cord. Now, while Mages use the Astral Plane to travel in the Umbra, Were-beasts use the &quot;Axis Mundi&quot;, the Three of Life for the same purpose, with different results. *Mages are &quot;lost in thoughts&quot; while werewolves are &quot;surfing in the synapses&quot;.<br /> <br /> In fact guys, I would appreciate some ideas! For instance, we have an autonomous nervous system, responsible for instance for our heart beating and the movements of our stomach, among others. I would like to have some grotesque and pretty physiological realms for those... Something raw, that felt... Alive <br /> <br /> If any of you liked those ideas so far and want to throw in some more, I would appreciate very much <br /> \u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-14T22:23:19-07:00","id":1535613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1535582-alternate-otherworlds-structure?p=1535587#post1535587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think this would not work. Look at the dreaming, its a mess no one wants to touch.<br /> <br /> My personal idea is that the otherworlds (can be called umbras why not) are the connected worlds of demon the fallen before there was just one after the fall.<br /> So every world is connected. Some things exist in many worlds. Whats a fire in the material plane could be a elemental in the spirit world, and could be a relic in the underworld and could be a commet in the horrizontal realm. Ofcourse things that that translate to multiple worlds would be rare.<br /> <br /> As a Lovecraft fan i would build those worlds as layers around the Abyss. Where in the abyss there are cthulhu monsters. Guarded by another monster that is reality itself in the form of omnipotent light. I dont mind keeping the 3 umbras as its hard as it is to imagine them sometimes but would keep them far less defined.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, if you're a fan of Lovecraft, I think you'll like my idea of a Spirit World based on the human mind. Just read my 2 previous posts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1535582-alternate-otherworlds-structure?p=1535590#post1535590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To me the greater problem is that they can't decide if Umbra is a place, a common name to several places, or a medium to reach places. <br /> I think <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar758_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"758\" data-vbnamecard=\"758\">Ramnesis</a> general idea is good, but I would throw away the very name &quot;Umbra&quot; and instead call those realities just &quot;Realms&quot;, with &quot;Astral&quot; and &quot;Spirit&quot; being classifications for realms.<br /> <br /> Also, specify the three &quot;Penumbrae&quot; as distinct mirror-realms, either with clear, practical means of interaction, or no interaction whatsoever.</div> </div> </div> </div> I didn't use any of the WoD names for my Spiritual Realms, since I wanted it to be original. Im also not a fan of hall fussy and confuse it all is, and that's one of the reasons that got me to start this project. I only used them here for the sake of facilitating communication. But I made each one of my Realms concise, coherent and with coherent &quot;pathways&quot;, or more precisely, with coherent interactions between them<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28035,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","user":"Magus Maximus","date":". 05-15-2024, 01:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-14T22:46:25-07:00","id":1535614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1535582-alternate-otherworlds-structure?p=1535590#post1535590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To me the greater problem is that they can't decide if Umbra is a place, a common name to several places, or a medium to reach places.<br /> <br /> I think <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar758_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"758\" data-vbnamecard=\"758\">Ramnesis</a> general idea is good, but I would throw away the very name &quot;Umbra&quot; and instead call those realities just &quot;Realms&quot;, with &quot;Astral&quot; and &quot;Spirit&quot; being classifications for realms.<br /> <br /> Also, specify the three &quot;Penumbrae&quot; as distinct mirror-realms, either with clear, practical means of interaction, or no interaction whatsoever.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's great! So, in my creation, as I briefly explained above, each realm is a sort of a &quot;shadow&quot; of an aspect of the human mind. So, the &quot;Penumbra&quot; (which I named as the &quot;Mirror Plane&quot;) is a &quot;shadow&quot; of our senses. It is the sensorial world basically. So, it sort of &quot;mimics&quot; the Material Plane but in very... Colourful ways, and everything is much more intense. And it is intrinsically connected to the &quot;Astral Plane&quot;, which is a &quot;shadow&quot; of our Conscious (and Pre Conscious) Mind, easily accessible by an infinite number of &quot;mirrors&quot; spread throughout it (those &quot;mirrors&quot; are actually the &quot;reflections&quot; of the &quot;membrane&quot; that permeates the entire Astral Plane).<br /> <br /> The Astral Plane is a huge &quot;membrane&quot; covering all other Realms. The Astral Plane represents our CONSCIOUSNESS. But, each realm is really, really deep - they represent fears, desires and so on. That &quot;membrane&quot; represents the fact that we can't really access our deepest thoughts; we don't readily interact with our Ego or Superego or I'd, but rather at the 'membrane thoughts&quot; that emerge in our conscious mind.<br /> <br /> If you jump from the Astral Plane and go over the membrane covering the &quot;Ego Realm&quot; (Paradise), you'll enter the realm that represents a &quot;healthy Ego&quot; (Paradise). You can see a &quot;reflection&quot; from Paradise in the membrane at the Astral Plane, but you can't see all of it without entering.<br /> <br /> <br /> Oh yes, I've also created another Realm; NIRVANA. This is, allegedly, the realm of &quot;Transcendence&quot;. This Realm is ruled by Buddha (big surprise), but you can see Buddha up there in the sky, but you can never reach him without being truly enlightened. Buddha will freely give you advice in your journey, but you cannot possibly reach Nirvana without being truly enlightened.<br /> <br /> Nirvana is a representation of the SOUL, therefore it is a sort of special realm that lies OUTSIDE... I'm not even sure that it should be called a &quot;Spiritual Realm&quot;, but something... More.<br /> <br /> - So, the idea I created have the Material Plane as a representation of the human body (therefore it is NOT a &quot;Spiritual World&quot; per se);<br /> - The Qlipphotic Plane as a representation of the OUTSIDE WORLD, outside from our minds and bodies; thus is also not strictly speaking a &quot;Spirit World&quot; but rather something more, something alien that can't be easily defined<br /> - Nirvana, which represents THE SOUL, thus it is not the Human Mind, but rather something more, something higher that also defies an easy classification and thus can't truly be defined as a &quot;mere&quot; &quot;Spirit World&quot;, but it's rather something more<br /> - And the &quot;Spirit World&quot; properly, which is a representation of the HUMAN MIND with all of its complexity and intricacies, which each Realm on it being an aspect of our minds. The main division here is between the &quot;Physiological Realms&quot; and the &quot;Psychological Realms&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-14T23:18:56-07:00","id":1535616,"title":"","content":"I still prefer to have an abyss in the center with godlike cthulhu creations traped. But the idea about the mind is quite smilar with what the original creators were going for. You could push the concept further and create a reptilian brain realm, a limbic system realm, an authority realm, a volition realm, a electrochemistry realm, a fight of flight realm, an anima realm and so on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-15T00:14:45-07:00","id":1535617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1535582-alternate-otherworlds-structure?p=1535616#post1535616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still prefer to have an abyss in the center with godlike cthulhu creations traped. But the idea about the mind is quite smilar with what the original creators were going for. You could push the concept further and create a reptilian brain realm, a limbic system realm, an authority realm, a volition realm, a electrochemistry realm, a fight of flight realm, an anima realm and so on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes yes, it has all of those. Reptilian brain and limbic will be part of the physiological realms. Anima/Animus are part of the Archetypes Realms, inside of the Collective Unconscious.<br /> <br /> Yes, it is similar to the original WoD, but I don't think they had this exact idea, not on a conscious way at least. I believe that what the creators did was a sublimation in a creative manner of subconscious ideas. That's perhaps why it is sometimes confuse, because it lacks a rational pragmatic organization. That's something I would like to fix","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-15T01:15:41-07:00","id":1535619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1535582-alternate-otherworlds-structure?p=1535590#post1535590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, specify the three &quot;Penumbrae&quot; as distinct mirror-realms, either with clear, practical means of interaction, or no interaction whatsoever.</div> </div> </div> </div>Generally I like the structure of the Umbra as it is, but I too would make the in-between realms (penumbrae) more interesting. A twilight realm that overlaps reality has so much more potential than just a coat of paint that colors the world in whatever concept lies beyond. I would add phenomena and 'physical' differences that allow interaction through those concepts that go further than just interaction with spirits, and give it more unique denizens and infrastructure, lore and history. The Shadowlands make a good example for this, although even those are underdeveloped for my liking.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-15T05:20:32-07:00","id":1535634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1535582-alternate-otherworlds-structure?p=1535617#post1535617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes yes, it has all of those. Reptilian brain and limbic will be part of the physiological realms. Anima/Animus are part of the Archetypes Realms, inside of the Collective Unconscious.<br /> <br /> Yes, it is similar to the original WoD, but I don't think they had this exact idea, not on a conscious way at least. I believe that what the creators did was a sublimation in a creative manner of subconscious ideas. That's perhaps why it is sometimes confuse, because it lacks a rational pragmatic organization. That's something I would like to fix</div> </div> </div> </div>So how exactly do you categorize it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-15T08:37:01-07:00","id":1535643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1535582-alternate-otherworlds-structure?p=1535634#post1535634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So how exactly do you categorize it?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry, I didn't understand. How do I categorize what?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-15T09:02:45-07:00","id":1535645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1535582-alternate-otherworlds-structure?p=1535643#post1535643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm sorry, I didn't understand. How do I categorize what?</div> </div> </div> </div>Your magic realms, i would like to see the details","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-15T11:10:00-07:00","id":1535654,"title":"","content":"From the point of view of the gaming table, I like the mental model. It makes the various realms easily accessible and understandable while leaving room for the mysterious. I also think that's a lot of the current structure of Otherworlds, with the High Umbra as thought, the Middle as feeling, and the Low as memory.<br /> <br /> That said I also think it is too humanistic. It gives the impression that everything is a reflection of humanity rather than its own entity. That's probably not the intention but it is the way my mind goes every time I go down that path.<br /> <br /> In that sense in my designs I would narrow the focus of the Astral to focus on the mind and have it contain thought, memory, and feeling. Likewise the Middle Umbra would focus on the animistic. All of the realms that only loosely fit into either I would move out into being full realms of their own, or in some cases, strange manifestations of the physical world.<br /> <br /> That said, one of my biggest problems is that without changing the Sphere system, there's a real need to keep many things as spirit realms, even if there's nothing really spiritual about them.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-15T12:59:44-07:00","id":1535666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1535582-alternate-otherworlds-structure?p=1535654#post1535654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From the point of view of the gaming table, I like the mental model. It makes the various realms easily accessible and understandable while leaving room for the mysterious. I also think that's a lot of the current structure of Otherworlds, with the High Umbra as thought, the Middle as feeling, and the Low as memory.<br /> <br /> That said I also think it is too humanistic. It gives the impression that everything is a reflection of humanity rather than its own entity. That's probably not the intention but it is the way my mind goes every time I go down that path.<br /> <br /> In that sense in my designs I would narrow the focus of the Astral to focus on the mind and have it contain thought, memory, and feeling. Likewise the Middle Umbra would focus on the animistic. All of the realms that only loosely fit into either I would move out into being full realms of their own, or in some cases, strange manifestations of the physical world.<br /> <br /> That said, one of my biggest problems is that without changing the Sphere system, there's a real need to keep many things as spirit realms, even if there's nothing really spiritual about them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did I get it right you want to take away the governence of other realms from the spirit sphere?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-15T13:32:54-07:00","id":1535669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1535582-alternate-otherworlds-structure?p=1535666#post1535666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Did I get it right you want to take away the governence of other realms from the spirit sphere?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. For the purposes of this discussion I'm not trying nerf or alter the way spheres work. That's sort of the problem. There's a lot in the Otherworlds that shouldn't be related to Spirit, but move too much of it and Spirit loses much of its purpose. <br /> <br /> Fortunately a lot of specific realms already function as physical realms so it shouldn't be too much of an issue. <br /> <br /> Also, I like your idea of things potentially existing in more than one phase of reality, and I think I'd like to keep part of that. Take Zeus for instance. He's potentially a real entity that once was more prominent in physical reality but has receded into the Otherworlds somewhere. There could also be a Zeus Archetype imprinted in the collective unconscious (presuming that's a part of the Astral). These aren't the same things, and yet they also can be. Powerful figures work quite well on multiple levels of existence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-15T14:32:02-07:00","id":1535677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1535582-alternate-otherworlds-structure#post1535582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is something I've been pondering recently. If we could toss out the existing structure of the otherworlds and remake it from scratch, without having to worry too much about other game lines, how would you do it?<br /> <br /> For my own part I'd probably:<br /> <br /> - Move away from a clearly defined gauntlet.<br /> - Make the astral, spirit, and under worlds very different things and not just different flavors of umbra.<br /> - Move more of the strangeness into the physical world.<br /> - Make more room for realms that don't actually fit anywhere but exist anyways<br /> <br /> I haven't gotten much further than that. What would you do?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is for Mage, right? Not \u201cThe World of Darkness\u201d; Mage. <br /> <br /> So we don't need to keep an Umbra that's consistent with the Garou, a Shadowlands that's consistent with Wraith, or a Dreaming that's consistent with Changeling; we can do our own thing without any concern about any of the other gamelines. Right? <br /> <br /> On the other hand, this <i>is </i>Mage, where a <i>huge </i>variety of belief systems coexist side by side; and ideally you can't pin down any one of them as being more true than any of the others. So chances are that if we can come up with something that satisfies Mage, it will naturally have something in it for the various other World of Darkness gamelines. That's not the <i>goal; </i>but it's likely to be the result. <br /> <br /> The following isn't a well-thought-out structure for the Otherworlds; it's more of a hodgepodge of ideas. <br /> <br /> I think what I'd do would probably be something like what Scion 2e does, with each Tradition, Convention, and Craft having a set of Reality Zones and Otherworlds of its own, in keeping with the cosmology favored by that Tradition. The Order of Hermes might have its Otherworlds organized into four planes of reality: Assiah (the Material), Yetzirah (the Astral), Briah (the Iconic), and Atziluth (the Spiritual). The Society of Ether would have the Hollow Earth and Etherspace. The Verbenae would have a Tree of Life, which its Nordic members would call Yggdrasil and who also identify as a bridge between the Nine Realms, of which Earth or Midgard is but one. The Virtual Adepts would have their Digital Web. Among the Traditions, the Akashayana would be the most likely to have Realms based on the human mind; and among the Conventions, the New World Order would be most likely to have access to psychic Realms. The Dreamspeakers, oddly, probably <i>wouldn't</i> have an Otherworld, per se; they'd deal with spirits that exist in and around <i>this</i> world. This in contrast to the Euthanatoi, who would be linked into the various Afterlives. And the Celestial Chorus would have access to Heaven and Hell. <br /> <br /> Getting to these Otherworlds would normally involve going to a suitable Reality Zone and bridging over to the Otherworld from there. Depending on the mage's Focus, it might be possible to \u201ccross over\u201d from other places; but even then, it would be easier to do so from an appropriate Reality Zone. <br /> <br /> Travel to Otherworlds wouldn't be the domain of any one Sphere; the Sphere you use would depend on the type of Otherworld you're going to. Correspondence can get a VA to the Digital Web, or a Void Engineer into Hyperspace; Entropy lets the Euthanatoi visit the Afterlives; Mind lets Akashics and NWO agents enter Mindscapes; Prime gives the Celestial Chorus access to Heaven and Hell. Forces and Matter could provide access to Elemental Planes. And Time could provide access to the past, the future, and alternate histories.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-15T15:54:37-07:00","id":1535689,"title":"","content":"Hmm how about a planet based concept?<br /> Each planet is a separate realm with ist own rules.<br /> Space is infinite so there are infinite worlds but those colse to us are baren cause the Technocracy destroyed them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-15T17:18:57-07:00","id":1535695,"title":"","content":"I would actually suggest the opposite: end the whole &quot;Space equal Umbra&quot; thing. The cosmology is more than complicated enough without this weird idea.<br /> <br /> Just state an end to Consensual Reality in opposition to a Space Reality Zone, not another dimension.<br /> <br /> This doesn't have to mean the Shard Realms and whatnot don't exist, just that the actual spheroids of matter exist in actual material reality, instead of Reality\u2122 being weirdly finite.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-16T06:26:59-07:00","id":1535721,"title":"","content":"I do like the idea of treating most of outer space as a vast shallowing. There should be regions where it isn't, of course--there are actual material aliens in some of the setting and it makes sense that the Gauntlet isn't unique to the solar system--but across a lot of the universe there's no difference between the worlds of spirit and flesh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28383-citrakayah","name":"Citrakayah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28383_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-16T08:48:26-07:00","id":1535735,"title":"","content":"I'm OK with a division between Conventional Space and Etherspace, where the latter deals with concepts of \u201cwhat's in the skies\u201d that don't conform to the scientific model; but I'd ditch the \u201cSpatial Horizon\u201d business: Conventional Space is <i>everywhere, </i>not just \u201cwherever humanity has explored\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-16T13:42:23-07:00","id":1535749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1535582-alternate-otherworlds-structure?p=1535677#post1535677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So we don't need to keep an Umbra that's consistent with the Garou, a Shadowlands that's consistent with Wraith, or a Dreaming that's consistent with Changeling; we can do our own thing without any concern about any of the other gamelines. Right?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the idea. We can leave room for them if we want, but for the purposes of this thread there's no reason to limit cosmology by what they need.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think what I'd do would probably be something like what Scion 2e does, with each Tradition, Convention, and Craft having a set of Reality Zones and Otherworlds of its own, in keeping with the cosmology favored by that Tradition. The Order of Hermes might have its Otherworlds organized into four planes of reality: Assiah (the Material), Yetzirah (the Astral), Briah (the Iconic), and Atziluth (the Spiritual). The Society of Ether would have the Hollow Earth and Etherspace. The Verbenae would have a Tree of Life, which its Nordic members would call Yggdrasil and who also identify as a bridge between the Nine Realms, of which Earth or Midgard is but one. The Virtual Adepts would have their Digital Web. Among the Traditions, the Akashayana would be the most likely to have Realms based on the human mind; and among the Conventions, the New World Order would be most likely to have access to psychic Realms. </div> </div> </div>I like this as it gives the impression that there is a lot out there and no one is even close to a complete map. I probably would have overlaps between broadly similar concepts, particularly things like the Astral realm. That doesn't mean everyone is going to the same part of that place, but it allows for conflicts in those regions. From a gameplay standpoint, it allows more interaction between mages in those regions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Dreamspeakers, oddly, probably <i>wouldn't</i> have an Otherworld, per se; they'd deal with spirits that exist in and around <i>this</i> world. </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <br /> This is making me picture the spirit world, in general in a more Orpheus sense, where there isn't a gauntlet between the spirit world and the physical world. Instead difficult lies in getting from there to the deeper, more specific spirit realms. That difficulty could be a barrier like a gauntlet or Orpheus' Stormwall, or it could be something else.<br /> <br /> This is giving me an impression as reality existing on multiple levels and shifting between realms is less about actual motion and more about changing phases or mental states. I'm not sure if that is a good thing or a bad thing, but I'm leaning towards good.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-16T14:08:34-07:00","id":1535751,"title":"","content":"Too many worlds can make meeting someone problematic. That can be seen in games like Nobilis and Amber. The solution those games give are powers that make it easy to find someone.<br /> Possible solutions are:<br /> - Substance vs Shadow: mages are more real so if you go into X reality then you are drawn twoards a reality where there are more mages.<br /> - Seeking (not actuall mage Seekings): powers to navigate to things and creatures and other worlds in the outer realms (spirit maybe?).<br /> I can already see mages attacking then jumping into their distinct realms the other party has no access.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-16T19:58:26-07:00","id":1535758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1535582-alternate-otherworlds-structure?p=1535735#post1535735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm OK with a division between Conventional Space and Etherspace, where the latter deals with concepts of \u201cwhat's in the skies\u201d that don't conform to the scientific model; but I'd ditch the \u201cSpatial Horizon\u201d business: Conventional Space is <i>everywhere, </i>not just \u201cwherever humanity has explored\u201d.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you go with the Shallowing model, those are just areas that are particularly affected by the magic of the Umbral realms. There are patches of the galaxy where the ether is present. You can breath it there. There are patches where it's vacuum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28383-citrakayah","name":"Citrakayah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28383_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-17T13:32:17-07:00","id":1535799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1535582-alternate-otherworlds-structure?p=1535645#post1535645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Your magic realms, i would like to see the details</div> </div> </div> </div>So, as I said, there are 4 major divisions:<br /> <br /> - Material Plane: represents our BODY<br /> - Qlipphotic Exterior: the &quot;anti-existance reality&quot; from where &quot;Things-Men-Were-Not-Meant-To-Know&quot; dwell. It represents the OUTSIDE WORLD (aka that which exists outside of our own minds)<br /> - Nirvana: the mysterious Transcendental Plane. It represents THE SOUL (whatever that means exactly, is highly debatable)<br /> - The Spirit Worlds: this one is the Spirit Reality &quot;proper&quot;. It represents THE MIND.<br /> <br /> Material Plane, Qlipphotic and Nirvana are NOT &quot;Spiritual&quot; realities. The Qlipphotic and Nirvana are not material either, but rather, something... More. Something... Alien.<br /> <br /> I'm actually building an entire setting for it, I'm considering, for example, to use a variation from Changeling the Lost, having the &quot;True Fae&quot; being Cthulhu-esque beings that come from the Qlipphotic Reality for example. I'm also rebuilding Vampires with a system that is pleasing me very much, upon which their &quot;Generation&quot; (which I call &quot;Blood Potency&quot;) increases over time, but as it increases, so too does their hunger, until they need to feed exclusively from other vampires, but they can willingly reduce their Blood Potency by creating new progeny, which also means that a vampire cannot create new Progeny in more than 5 years at a time, and many other changes, including Vampiric Families and many more.<br /> <br /> But that's besides the point. The point is that &quot;Spirit Worlds&quot; are related to the human mind, anything other than that is either the material world or something completely alien and possibly impossible to define (by human words at least). Nirvana, likewise, is impossible to define. Maybe it isn't even truly a &quot;place&quot;, but rather just a state of &quot;oneness&quot; with the whole... Whatever that may be.<br /> <br /> As for the Spirit Worlds, there's going to be a separation between &quot;Physiological Realms&quot; and &quot;Psychological Realms&quot; (obviously, that's not what they're named, I'm just explaining how they work). I liked Ramnesis idea of having an animistic &quot;Middle Umbra&quot; and a &quot;Mental Landscape&quot; &quot;High Umbra&quot;. That's indeed more or less how this is going to work. The &quot;Physiological Realms&quot; will be more animistic, primal, more &quot;material&quot; in essence, since they are connected to our physiology. The most famous Realm in this section will the &quot;Spirit Wilds&quot; or the &quot;Primal Wilds&quot;, upon which everything in the material Plane gets a more vibrant reflection. The other focal point will be the &quot;Axis Mundi&quot;, which is a huge, cosmic Mountain/Three that connects all the Realms in the &quot;Physiological&quot; Spirit Worlds, and represents our Spinal Cord. The &quot;Axis Mundi&quot; will have branches touching the Material Plane, which represents the nerves.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> Juxtaposing the &quot;Physiological Realms&quot; will be the &quot;Psychological Realms&quot;, which will exist in a different layer of reality but working together. It's like having the Hardware and the Software of a computer <br /> <br /> PS: I'm also considering the possibility of using a computer as the basis for the concept instead of the human mind<br /> <br /> Getting from one layer to another is possible, but not easy at all. It's like trying to change your &quot;quantum package&quot; if you're trying to &quot;change between universes&quot; if there is a multiverse with infinite universes.<br /> <br /> Or, in another way to explain, it's like trying to pinpoint a single synaptic signal to what it means... For example, if you place an electric detector in the nerve that is connected to your eyes, the detector will detect the presence of an electrical signal, but that's still worlds away from being able to translate those electric pulses into an image.<br /> <br /> Much the same holds true. Traveling though the &quot;Physiological Realms&quot; is like traveling along the synapses inside our brains and nerves. Traveling through the &quot;Psycological Realms&quot; however is like traveling through your thoughts. So, both realities work together but they have a very distinct EMERGENT Pattern. One &quot;Spiritual Synapse&quot; for instance, could be &quot;traveling&quot; throughout the Axis Mundi (Spinal Cord), activating &quot;fear&quot; responses in the Spirit Worlds, but that would have very distinct interactions throughout the &quot;Psychological Realms&quot;. In fact, a veteran &quot;traveler&quot; could jump from one another in order to reach very different destinations in either one of the realities, but that's not an easy task - it would be like trying to &quot;surf in your own synapses&quot; until you reach an specific set of neural configurations that is responsible for storing an specific memory that you want to uncover.<br /> <br /> Thus, the &quot;Physiological Realms&quot; are more primal, it feels alive and somewhat &quot;material&quot;, while the &quot;Psychological&quot; ones are more &quot;ethereal&quot; and abstract. Coincidentally, that luckily lands itself easily towards a natural division for an &quot;Umbra for Mages and an Umbra for Were-beasts&quot;.<br /> <br /> The Psychological Realms have the Astral Plane, representing the Pre Conscious Mind, forming a &quot;Membrane&quot; that covers the entirety of the Spirit Worlds. The Astral Plane is accessible using Mind Magics, but in order to step into any other Realm, you need Spirit Magic. The Astral Plane is therefore a sort of &quot;Axis Mundi&quot; for the Psychological Realms.<br /> <br /> As for the Realms themselves, it would be an herculean job to name them all, but for the Physiological, I'll still create those for the Brain, Reptilian and Mammal brain, nerves, Autonomous System and so on.<br /> <br /> So far, I worked a bit more on the &quot;Psychological&quot; Realms. For example, the &quot;Akashic Records&quot; is an endless Library Realm that contains the knowledge about... Everything. This Realm represents the MEMORY, and is ruled by Thoth, the Egyptian God of Magic and Knowledge. Then you have the Dreamlands, that resides in the Subconscious, ruled by Morpheus.<br /> <br /> Oh yes, the psychological realms have 3 layers, the Conscious Mind, called &quot;Mirror Realm&quot; (call it &quot;Penumbra if you will), the Subconscious and the Unconscious.<br /> <br /> The Subconscious holds the Dreamlands, Akashic Records, and most famously, &quot;Heaven and Hell&quot; realms, which are not single realms, but rather the interactions between Id, Ego and Superego. When harmonious, you're in &quot;Paradise&quot;. When those are in disharmony, you're in &quot;Hell&quot;. For example, the &quot;Harmonious Id&quot; is the &quot;Ethereal Plane&quot;, the center of creation, ruled by Vishnu and the Holy Spirit. The harmonious Ego is Paradise, ruled by Bhrama and Jesus Christ. And the Harmonious Superego is the &quot;Primal Crucible&quot;, ruled by Shiva the Destroyer and God the Father, upon which the most iconic spirit is the Phoenix bird getting rebirthed from its ashes. The Ethereal Plane is the literal center of creation, where everything is created, &quot;Paradise&quot; is the center of all the order in the Universe, and the Primal Crucible is where everything faces final judgement and ultimately, renewal, acceptance and forgiveness.<br /> <br /> Note that this also follows the Triad of Chaos, Order and Destruction too, so I also added that.<br /> <br /> There's finally one final section of &quot;Heaven&quot;, which is the mysterious Realm of &quot;Integration&quot;, where all those 3 forces are integrated into perfect Harmony. Legend says that this place is ruled by The One, and it is the Gateway towards Nirvana<br /> <br /> &quot;Hell&quot; on the other hand is when those 3 forces are in disharmony. I'd have to check my notes, but Hell is actually divided into 7 different &quot;sections&quot;, each representing disharmony between 2 of those aspects besides the main theme. Therefore, there's a &quot;hell&quot; for a disharmonious Id, but also the &quot;intersectional&quot; hells for Id+Ego and Id+Superego disharmony, for a total of 6 Realms. For instance, the Realm properly named as &quot;Hell&quot; represents a disharmonious Id, thus it is a Realm of violence, lust, gluttony and desire without control, while &quot;Purgatory&quot; represents a disharmonious Superego, a place where you can never find rest and is constantly tormented by your mistakes and flaws.<br /> <br /> Finally, the &quot;Lower Realms&quot; (the collective &quot;Hells&quot;) have the Realm of &quot;Penitence&quot;, which is their own integration Realm. The legend says that, after going through the Realm of Penitence, a Spirit (or perhaps a &quot;Soul&quot;) could eventually reach the Primal Crucible (in Heaven), and be finally &quot;cleansed&quot; after standing judgment.<br /> <br /> There is also the Underworld, which is a very specific Realm for Memory. Unlike the Akashic Records library however, this is where memories are... Deleted. This is the Realm of the Forgotten things, towards which the final destination is Oblivion. The ghosts of the dead dwell here, soon to be, inevitably, forgotten. But they are not the only ones. Many categories of Spirits that are under &quot;risk of extinction&quot; will dwell their last eras in here too.<br /> <br /> From Oblivion, nothing returns. It's like a memory that is forever erased from the mind. Those Spirits that fall here get trapped, and usually get transformed over time.<br /> <br /> Banshees, for instance, are terrible Spirits that come from the Dreamlands and fall into the Underworld, turning into terrifying Spirits preying on the living and the dead alike. Sometimes even &quot;celestials&quot; (Spirits from the Heavens) or &quot;demons&quot; (Spirits from Hell) can be find in the Underworld, sometimes changing into terrible &quot;Fallen Angels&quot; or repentant beings trying to help the dead.<br /> <br /> On rare occasions, Spirits from the Underworld escape and find themselves on other Realms. The Dreamlands seen to have a particular connection with the Underworld, since among all the Plasmics that dwell in there (Spirits other than the ghosts of the Dead), one of the most common are the Banshees. Other than that, while it is uncommon but not unheard of, many Plasmics have managed to escape to the Dreamlands, where they'll usually turn into Great Nightmares, powerfully malevolent Dream Spirits.<br /> <br /> That connection represents suppressed memories, who commonly appear in abstract and archetypical ways during our dreams. So much so that there are very few spirits with a dual nature, that exist both in the Underworld and in the Dreamlands, usually being Great Nightmares that plague these Realms. The question &quot;could those be the Malfeans?' I'll leave to the STs to answer.<br /> <br /> Then, the higher level of the Psychological Spirit Worlds is the Archetypal Unconscious. This is a place of abstraction. In here, you'll find many Archetype Realms, my favorite ones being the Holy Mother, ruled by the Virgin Mary and Gaia, the Dark Mother, ruled by Lilith and Kali, the Wise King, ruled by King Solomon, the Tyrant, ruled by Chronus, Anima, ruled by Psyche, Animus, ruled by Eros, The Shadow (The Shadowlands), ruled by Satan, the Trickster, ruled by Loki, the Warrior, ruled by Hercules and many many others.<br /> <br /> That's the basic structure of it all so far. I have detailed many many more realms, but this is too long already, and I've detailed each thoroughly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-17T13:51:30-07:00","id":1535800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1535582-alternate-otherworlds-structure?p=1535654#post1535654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From the point of view of the gaming table, I like the mental model. It makes the various realms easily accessible and understandable while leaving room for the mysterious. I also think that's a lot of the current structure of Otherworlds, with the High Umbra as thought, the Middle as feeling, and the Low as memory.<br /> <br /> That said I also think it is too humanistic. It gives the impression that everything is a reflection of humanity rather than its own entity. That's probably not the intention but it is the way my mind goes every time I go down that path.<br /> <br /> In that sense in my designs I would narrow the focus of the Astral to focus on the mind and have it contain thought, memory, and feeling. Likewise the Middle Umbra would focus on the animistic. All of the realms that only loosely fit into either I would move out into being full realms of their own, or in some cases, strange manifestations of the physical world.<br /> <br /> That said, one of my biggest problems is that without changing the Sphere system, there's a real need to keep many things as spirit realms, even if there's nothing really spiritual about them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the &quot;too humanistic&quot; part is true. First of all, we need to take into consideration that animism is an anthropomorphization of nature. Therefore, every single mystical or religious idea in history is inevitably &quot;human-centric&quot;. Because that's how the primitive and ancient humans tried to make sense of a senseless nature, by attributing human characteristics to it.<br /> <br /> Trying to get rid of such a &quot;tendency&quot; would funnily mean to move away from a &quot;mystical&quot; background and towards a more mechanicist viewpoint; in essence, it would be a sort of &quot;scientificization&quot; of the myths, where instead of having nature with human characteristics, they are viewed as impersonal forces.<br /> <br /> Sure thing, if the spirit world was real and approachable towards some sort of scientific method, that would probably be more like the answer; on top of our material nature that doesn't care about humans at all and that neither hates nor loves us but instead doesn't think or feel at all, and therefore wouldn't miss us if we were extinct, we then would have yet another layer of nature that is completely oblivious to us or towards itself.<br /> <br /> But that's not how mystical views are formed, since they are all of them absolutely human-centric.<br /> <br /> That however, was not behind the reasoning I used to adopt such a model - and neither does it represents the WoD Umbra.<br /> <br /> As I have already said ad nauseum, WoD is a heavily Gnostic/Hermetic setting. If the writers did so because they are secretly cultists gathering under auspicious moons in the middle of the night wearing cloaks and sacrificing animals to their hermetic Masters, or if the writers did so after extensive research into esoteric literature, which inevitably would end up ending into Gnostic/Theosophical/Hermetic literature, since it is an ancient, prolific and syncretic set of beliefs that have ended up &quot;infecting&quot; many other currents of theology and philosophy (for example, Immanuel Kant and Hegel works drip Gnosticism throughout their entire works), that is debatable. If I were to bet, I would say that the writers were searching esoteric literature and eventually ended up with a copy of the &quot;Corpus Hermeticum&quot; and from there on, everything they wrote started to be done following the mantra &quot;As Above, So Bellow&quot;.<br /> <br /> Be that as it may, WoD is absolutely Gnostic/Hermetic throughout all of its pages, up to the point that Vampires were created by a being that can only be described as the evil Demiurge of Gnosticism.<br /> <br /> So, this idea that the Spirit Worlds function as the &quot;human mind&quot;, is absolutely rooted under Gnostic/Hermetic thought. It is in the essence of &quot;As Above, so Bellow&quot; - which means at the end exactly that, the human mind is a reflection of &quot;God's mind&quot;. Because, as above (God), so bellow (human).<br /> <br /> Hegelian dialectics for instance is purely Gnostic thinking. As is the immaterialism of Emmanuel Kant. It's the idea that EVERYTHING is just &quot;God's Mind&quot;.<br /> <br /> In Gnostic mythology, although I'm heavily simplifying, first there was God, and God was just mind, it was pure intellect, pure mind.<br /> <br /> And, because everything was God's mind, everything that existed was essentially a byproduct of God's imagination.<br /> <br /> Yes, Gnosticism is solipsism (or distilled and twice pure narcissism) elevated to infinite.<br /> <br /> Eventually, God begun to mistake his imagination with reality, unable to understand that the things around himself/herself/itself were just products of its imagination, not the reality of things.<br /> <br /> Then God got &quot;shattered&quot;, and each shatter became a &quot;soul&quot; - that's us. We are fragments of the divine.<br /> <br /> The bigger fragment, however, is called the &quot;Demiurge&quot;, and is the God of the Bible (and plenty of other Gods from other religions), and the Demiurge is our enemy, he is our imprisoner. The Demiurge, being that he is a being with a larger portion of the fragments of the original God, enjoyed this fake reality created by the imagination of God, and seeks to rule over it, and the last thing that the Demiurge wants is for the other shards of God's soul to reunite and acknowledge that they are God and that everything that is isn't real, is just imagination. So, the Demiurge created the Material World as a prison for the shards of God, so that they can't awaken for the truth.<br /> <br /> Luckily for the Gnostics/Hermetics, they can &quot;awaken&quot; due to &quot;Divine Revelation&quot; (that's literally what the word &quot;Gnosis&quot; in Greek means, Divine Revelation. No, it is NOT &quot;knowledge&quot;, but rather specifically &quot;knowledge acquired by DIVINE REVELATION) and the guidance of their &quot;Hermetic Masters&quot;, to which they claim that figures like Jesus or Buddha were just a few. And their purpose is to guide the whole of humanity towards a &quot;collective awakening&quot;, upon which we would all come to the realization that we are in fact God, and then we would transcend the prison of the Demiurge.<br /> <br /> That's the origin of those concepts.<br /> <br /> As you can see, all this mythology seem to be an almost perfect fit for WoD - again, I believe that this has been accidental, but if you see primarily Mage and Demon, there's no denying, but even the others are pretty close to it.<br /> <br /> That's probably why the Umbra has such a configuration; I also have to say, there's many ideas present on the WoD Umbra that seem to be taken directly from the real life Corpus Hermeticum book. I have some knowledge about that, so I can say as much. Sure, there's some artistic and creative modifications, but it is pretty closely aligned with the real world Hermetic mythology. No doubt this has been one of the major inspirations for the games.<br /> <br /> In my case, it wasn't so much due to fascination towards hermetic mythos, even thou I liked the idea of modelling it with some sprinkles of &quot;as above, so below&quot;, but I just liked the concept of having the entirety of the universe as a living, thinking entity (God/Nature/whatever). There are, for instance, some theories that the Universe in a quantum level, behaves exactly like a Quantum Computer... Because, the random quantum fluctuations of particles, behave EXACTLY like a Quantum Computer.<br /> <br /> This would imply that... That the Universe THINKS. Like a cosmic mind.<br /> <br /> So, I decided to use the human mind to model this &quot;Cosmic Mind&quot; because the Human Mind is the only parameter that we know. We do not have access to alien minds in order to try to do so. I could perhaps use a computer as a model, maybe that would also work.<br /> <br /> I don't have a problem with it being &quot;human-centric&quot; thou, because all mystical thought is human-centric in nature, as I already explained","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28035,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","user":"Magus Maximus","date":". 05-17-2024, 05:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-17T15:12:12-07:00","id":1535802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1535582-alternate-otherworlds-structure?p=1535695#post1535695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would actually suggest the opposite: end the whole &quot;Space equal Umbra&quot; thing. The cosmology is more than complicated enough without this weird idea.<br /> <br /> Just state an end to Consensual Reality in opposition to a Space Reality Zone, not another dimension.<br /> <br /> This doesn't have to mean the Shard Realms and whatnot don't exist, just that the actual spheroids of matter exist in actual material reality, instead of Reality\u2122 being weirdly finite.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's how I'll do it. Space is just space. Empty space. In fact, in most of it, there's no Spirit on them. They are just big blobs of rocks or gas.<br /> <br /> Spirit will be a direct byproduct of mind. Spirits will only exist where there is an active consciousness behind. Aka, in order for &quot;Spirits&quot; to exist, there's the need for a conscious &quot;God&quot; giving them substance.<br /> <br /> That plays nicely for the idea of &quot;Divine Immaterialism&quot; from Kant, but it also plays nice with the more scientificist (not to confuse with &quot;scientific&quot;) idea of the Universe as a simulation, or of the Universe behaving like a Quantum Computer.<br /> <br /> I'm still playing with the idea of alien worlds. Would another planet, with intelligent life, have its own &quot;Umbra&quot;? I'm strongly leaning towards &quot;YES!&quot;. So, Earth has a &quot;Spirit World&quot;, which is not exactly connected to the physical blob of rocks we call &quot;Planet Terra&quot;, but rather it is connected to the human mind.<br /> <br /> The Aliens living in Alpha Centaur however, will have their own &quot;Umbra&quot; connected to their own alien minds, and that functions under entirely different premisses. Heck, alien &quot;Mages&quot; could access their own Umbra with their own version of Spirit Sphere, but their Spirit Sphere would be absolutely useless in trying to access our &quot;Umbra&quot;, and vice versa.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, between here and Alpha Centaur, there's just a gazillion of very material empty space and a few very material floating rocks and gases.<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-17T15:24:24-07:00","id":1535803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1535582-alternate-otherworlds-structure?p=1535749#post1535749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's the idea. We can leave room for them if we want, but for the purposes of this thread there's no reason to limit cosmology by what they need.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I like this as it gives the impression that there is a lot out there and no one is even close to a complete map. I probably would have overlaps between broadly similar concepts, particularly things like the Astral realm. That doesn't mean everyone is going to the same part of that place, but it allows for conflicts in those regions. From a gameplay standpoint, it allows more interaction between mages in those regions.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> This is making me picture the spirit world, in general in a more Orpheus sense, where there isn't a gauntlet between the spirit world and the physical world. Instead difficult lies in getting from there to the deeper, more specific spirit realms. That difficulty could be a barrier like a gauntlet or Orpheus' Stormwall, or it could be something else.<br /> <br /> This is giving me an impression as reality existing on multiple levels and shifting between realms is less about actual motion and more about changing phases or mental states. I'm not sure if that is a good thing or a bad thing, but I'm leaning towards good.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, my model won't rely on physical motion; in realms made of abstraction made concrete, moving in space is meaningless. Instead, navigation in the Spirit Worlds will be exactly that, changing phases and/or mental states. I'm leaning towards having &quot;changing phases&quot; be a thing for the &quot;Physiological Realms&quot; while mental states being the thing for the &quot;Psychological Realms&quot;.<br /> <br /> So, since you enter the Spirit Worlds by the Astral Plane or by the Mirror Realm which ends up connecting you towards the Astral Plane, and the Astral Plane is pure thought, EVERYTHING that you think is manifested in the Astral Plane. In fact, the Astral Plane reflects everything that EVERYBODY thinks. So, when you think of something, you will be guided in that direction.<br /> <br /> I envisioned the Astral Plane as an endless sky, with a membrane covering infinite realms, and the &quot;winds of thought&quot; blowing up constantly.<br /> <br /> I was in the process of creating tables and game mechanics systems for dealing with navigation over the Astral Plane. Things like critical failures in concentration or meditation would mean an intrusive thought sneaking into your mind, which could risk blowing you towards realms like the 7 Hells, the Shadowlands or the Underworld or similar, but even towards nightmarish parts of the Dreamlands and so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-17T16:53:09-07:00","id":1535811,"title":"","content":"Your model made me think of other worlds in Nobilis, There you have 5 types of other worlds:<br /> - Spirit Realm - another dimention tied to the material world. Everything has a spirit and those spirits live here.<br /> - Material worlds - mundane physical realms that grow like fruit on the great tree of life.<br /> - Hell - Hell is in the roots of the tree. Its a domain of caring and suffering.<br /> - Havens - Havens are a domain of light and uncaring perfection<br /> - Chancels - personal realms of individual gods with their own subjective access ways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-17T17:40:24-07:00","id":1535819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1535582-alternate-otherworlds-structure?p=1535811#post1535811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your model made me think of other worlds in Nobilis, There you have 5 types of other worlds:<br /> - Spirit Realm - another dimention tied to the material world. Everything has a spirit and those spirits live here.<br /> - Material worlds - mundane physical realms that grow like fruit on the great tree of life.<br /> - Hell - Hell is in the roots of the tree. Its a domain of caring and suffering.<br /> - Havens - Havens are a domain of light and uncaring perfection<br /> - Chancels - personal realms of individual gods with their own subjective access ways.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting. I was thinking on ways to add more depth towards the Qlipphotic Outer Reality, I think placing the Alien &quot;True Fae&quot; from Changeling the Lost there is one step, but I would like some more. Sure thing, cosmic horrors, yes, but what else?<br /> <br /> Or maybe, the UNKNOWABLE should remain like that, unknowable.<br /> <br /> The Qlipphotic Outer Reality shouldn't directly interact with the rest thou... Now, in keeping with the analogy, that is, it represents the exterior world (out of the mind), then nobody can really cross the barrier - much like a person can't enter your mind in the real life, nor can your thoughts get out of your mind and interact with the outside world.<br /> <br /> There are however... Whispers. We do, after all, get imput from our senses about the exterior world. Thus, if Cthulhu lives in the Qlipphotic Outer Reality, he can't cross into ours, but he can surely whisper in &quot;God's ears&quot;. Just like a bad actor can manipulate a person to her own detriment, instilling thoughts that aren't her on, sometimes &quot;Voices from the Beyond&quot; can reach willing ears... And that's how the Nefandi are born.<br /> <br /> I had this idea about the &quot;Whispers from Beyond&quot;, capable of driving spirits mad from that to time, as a sort of &quot;outside influence&quot;. Like that &quot;friend&quot; convincing you to use drugs...<br /> <br /> Since in this model the Realms are representations of aspects of the mind, the Spirits denizens of that reality are like thoughts, and a &quot;Whisper from Beyond&quot; is capable of traveling the Realms, driving spirits mad and twisting them (representing external influences shaping bad thoughts).<br /> <br /> Those could appear as cracks in reality from which utter madness vent forward.<br /> <br /> The pits of Hell would be filled with those cracks, from which demons imprison other spirits and breed new demons from.<br /> <br /> That also gave me the idea of dividing the types of Nefandi - those that were corrupted by demons from Hell itself would be the &quot;common&quot; Infernalists, but the ones driven mad by the &quot;Whispers from Beyond&quot; would be the Others. The Cthulhu-esque cultists that follow alien voices in their heads.<br /> <br /> I'm just having a bit of a hard time to (re)create the third kind. I'm not a fan of the &quot;Wyrm&quot; at all. I have no intention of having an anthropomorphized conscious deity representing cosmic destruction. And no, Shiva the Destroyer that oversees the Primal Crucible is NOT that, he is just a powerful spirit Archetype.<br /> <br /> I do like however to have the Mage Triad, because I'm also dividing the Universe between Id, Ego and Superego, and they can be easily connected to Chaos, Order and Destruction. Thus, the Nefandi Infernalists could be easily connected towards Order or Ego (ah, the infamous Lawful Evil Devils). While the Nefandic Others are connected to Chaos or Id.<br /> <br /> But I'm not sure about Destruction/Superego. Maybe... Maybe they could be connected to the Shadowlands, which is connected to the Jungian concept of the Shadow, our negative self. Maybe this could work. What y'all think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-17T18:38:30-07:00","id":1535833,"title":"","content":"If you want to make your cosmology Jungian, make it Jungian. If you want to make it Freudian, make it Freudian. And if you want to make it Triatic, make it Triatic.<br /> <br /> You can have minor groups of realms that explore other ideas, but while doing your main thing you must be more focused. Otherwise you'll never achieve the goal you keep expanding to embrace everything.<br /> <br /> Also, keep always in mind what function each piece has as a game component. However you describe them, each piece of your cosmology is only relevant when it interact with the game in some way, and you have to think what that will be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-17T21:36:22-07:00","id":1535843,"title":"","content":"I would have the cosmology be composed of the physical universe, the astral plane, and unmanifest existence. You could have classic animist spirits dwelling in an incorporeal form in the physical universe. Most other types of spirits, such as gods, angels, and demons, would reside in the astral. Pretty much every distinct spiritual realm would compose a segment of the astral. Importantly, the astral would be non-physical, but it would still have manifest forms that would be fairly straightforward for a human to understand. Finally, there would be unmanifest existence. This would be the dwelling place for unconditioned entities, and would thus reside outside of the realm of game statistics. It would not be a place, but a state of being. The Spirit Sphere would be used for interacting with spirits in the physical world, and for interacting with the astral. The Mind Sphere would also have some uses that related to the astral. <br /> <br /> I think that that covers all of the essentials whilst still leaving things undefined enough for a wide variety of paradigms to be compatible with it. It would not work for all paradigms, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28352-verlan","name":"Verlan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-18T02:23:33-07:00","id":1535846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1535582-alternate-otherworlds-structure?p=1535819#post1535819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Interesting. I was thinking on ways to add more depth towards the Qlipphotic Outer Reality, I think placing the Alien &quot;True Fae&quot; from Changeling the Lost there is one step, but I would like some more. Sure thing, cosmic horrors, yes, but what else?<br /> <br /> Or maybe, the UNKNOWABLE should remain like that, unknowable.<br /> <br /> The Qlipphotic Outer Reality shouldn't directly interact with the rest thou... Now, in keeping with the analogy, that is, it represents the exterior world (out of the mind), then nobody can really cross the barrier - much like a person can't enter your mind in the real life, nor can your thoughts get out of your mind and interact with the outside world.<br /> <br /> There are however... Whispers. We do, after all, get imput from our senses about the exterior world. Thus, if Cthulhu lives in the Qlipphotic Outer Reality, he can't cross into ours, but he can surely whisper in &quot;God's ears&quot;. Just like a bad actor can manipulate a person to her own detriment, instilling thoughts that aren't her on, sometimes &quot;Voices from the Beyond&quot; can reach willing ears... And that's how the Nefandi are born.<br /> <br /> I had this idea about the &quot;Whispers from Beyond&quot;, capable of driving spirits mad from that to time, as a sort of &quot;outside influence&quot;. Like that &quot;friend&quot; convincing you to use drugs...<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>In Lovecrafts stories the Other Gods need blood and sacrafice to manifest.It could be even implied that the steamengine ship defeated Cthulhu cause it destroyed his form makim him lose blood and becoming immaterial again and imprisoned in the beyond once more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-21T13:29:30-07:00","id":1536078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1535582-alternate-otherworlds-structure?p=1535833#post1535833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want to make your cosmology Jungian, make it Jungian. If you want to make it Freudian, make it Freudian. And if you want to make it Triatic, make it Triatic.<br /> <br /> You can have minor groups of realms that explore other ideas, but while doing your main thing you must be more focused. Otherwise you'll never achieve the goal you keep expanding to embrace everything.<br /> <br /> Also, keep always in mind what function each piece has as a game component. However you describe them, each piece of your cosmology is only relevant when it interact with the game in some way, and you have to think what that will be.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is one of the problems I run into with the current cosmology. The High Umbra is sometimes the Astral, sometimes an alternate spirit world, and sometimes the place for things that have fallen out of the physical world. <br /> <br /> I think there\u2019s a place for things that are metaphysically present regardless of belief or chronicle, like the spirit world and astral, and places that are created by the consensus or by powerful entities. I\u2019d rather keep them largely separate though<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-21T18:43:39-07:00","id":1536087,"title":"","content":"Didn't he reform from being rammed, and the surviving sailors only escaped because R'lyeh sank beneath the waves again, returning him to his long sleep/imprisonment?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-21T23:27:22-07:00","id":1536093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1535582-alternate-otherworlds-structure?p=1536087#post1536087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Didn't he reform from being rammed, and the surviving sailors only escaped because R'lyeh sank beneath the waves again, returning him to his long sleep/imprisonment?</div> </div> </div> </div>Thats one of the theories. But the idea is in my opinion wrong for 2 reasons:<br /> 1. He already left the city<br /> 2. He never really was in the city. The other gods (all of them) exist in the abyss like prison in the centre of the universe.<br /> <br /> Therefore what i believe is:<br /> 1. That was not Cthulhu, just a &quot;star spawn&quot; (term created by chaosium, orginal cthulhu race is &quot;the great old ones&quot;. And whats called great old ones by chaosium in reality is Other gods like Nyarlathotep)<br /> or<br /> 2. Thats Cthulhu that was summoned filled with blood sacrifice. Got hit, lost a lot too much of blood and while it did not hurt him it made his connection to the world weak enough to be banished after a while.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-22T11:36:11-07:00","id":1536104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1535582-alternate-otherworlds-structure?p=1536093#post1536093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thats one of the theories. But the idea is in my opinion wrong for 2 reasons:<br /> 1. He already left the city<br /> 2. He never really was in the city. The other gods (all of them) exist in the abyss like prison in the centre of the universe.<br /> <br /> Therefore what i believe is:<br /> 1. That was not Cthulhu, just a &quot;star spawn&quot; (term created by chaosium, orginal cthulhu race is &quot;the great old ones&quot;. And whats called great old ones by chaosium in reality is Other gods like Nyarlathotep)<br /> or<br /> 2. Thats Cthulhu that was summoned filled with blood sacrifice. Got hit, lost a lot too much of blood and while it did not hurt him it made his connection to the world weak enough to be banished after a while.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even going only by the story, I really don't get any vibe that it was anything like that. As far as the story goes, Cthulhu and R'lyeh both sunk because reasons (the stars weren't aligned any more) and the boat just got lucky.<br /> <br /> Lovecraft never stated that all Other Gods were with Azatoth, or even that he were being overly coherent in his use of such terms. He was not trying to build a cohesive setting, he was just writing horror stories.<br /> <br /> Everything we have on Cthulhu says he sleeps on the sunken city, that his race once roamed Earth with impunity, and that humanity is completely hopeless against them. Your theory may work for your headcanon, but it doesn't seems to be at all what Lovecraft either wrote or intended.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-22T12:19:06-07:00","id":1536109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1535582-alternate-otherworlds-structure?p=1536104#post1536104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even going only by the story, I really don't get any vibe that it was anything like that. As far as the story goes, Cthulhu and R'lyeh both sunk because reasons (the stars weren't aligned any more) and the boat just got lucky.<br /> <br /> Lovecraft never stated that all Other Gods were with Azatoth, or even that he were being overly coherent in his use of such terms. He was not trying to build a cohesive setting, he was just writing horror stories.<br /> <br /> Everything we have on Cthulhu says he sleeps on the sunken city, that his race once roamed Earth with impunity, and that humanity is completely hopeless against them. Your theory may work for your headcanon, but it doesn't seems to be at all what Lovecraft either wrote or intended.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is false. The blood part is my headcannon yes but he did write about it enough to make it legit. Azatoth is an Other God and all of the Other Gods reside outside (the outside or the void) realspace and can only be summoned via blood sacrafices. Specifically Cthulhu &quot;when the stars are right&quot; can be summoned from R'yleh<br /> &quot;It needed nurishment of sacrifice, for it was a god. Of course it coudnt get It sort of sacrifices witch it used to have in Its day, for such things dont exist now. Biut there were other things which might do. The blood is the life, you know. Even the lemures and elementals that are older than the earth will come when blood od men and beasts is offered under the right conditions&quot; - horror in the museum.<br /> <br /> The Cthulhu chosen race lives in R'lyeh. The are also mentioned as the Great Old Ones (a title that chaosium gave to the &quot;weaker&quot; Other gods). When the Olympian gods have sunken the continent with R'lyeh cthulhu preserved them with magic (too lazy to quote but its in Call of Cthulhu). The city will rise again awakening them if its up and if Cthulhu will be there. Cthulhu does not live in R'lyeh. Its more of a portal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-23T13:58:07-07:00","id":1536167,"title":"","content":"Azatoth is surrounded by other gods, but there is no mention to those being all such gods. Azathoth lives in the center of the universe, Yog-Sothoth comes from outside of reality, Hastur live in a material world, if a very strange one. There's no indication that this is different for most others, like Shub-Niggurath or Tsathogua.<br /> <br /> Cthulhu isn't even always referred as a god, being instead a cleric to the actual gods in some instances, Lovecraft himself didn't use the term in such a rigid manner, this was not the point.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying you can't interpret it in the way you're doing, but it isn't what The Call of Cthulhu indicates in any way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-23T23:00:52-07:00","id":1536191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1535582-alternate-otherworlds-structure?p=1536167#post1536167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Azatoth is surrounded by other gods, but there is no mention to those being all such gods. Azathoth lives in the center of the universe, Yog-Sothoth comes from outside of reality, Hastur live in a material world, if a very strange one. There's no indication that this is different for most others, like Shub-Niggurath or Tsathogua.<br /> <br /> Cthulhu isn't even always referred as a god, being instead a cleric to the actual gods in some instances, Lovecraft himself didn't use the term in such a rigid manner, this was not the point.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying you can't interpret it in the way you're doing, but it isn't what The Call of Cthulhu indicates in any way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hastur lives in the dreamlands and is not actually an Other God but a dreamland entity. (take note that the gods of earth: olympian, egiptian, mayan and so on also live in the dreamlands).<br /> Azatoth lives in the center of reality and that is ... drumroll the void<br /> Yog sototh is the ultimate gate, that is a barier of light around the void and is said to BE the universe itself<br /> Cthulhu is refered as a god many times and hes called the priest of the great old ones (hes people not great old ones in chaosium version). And he is called a priest cause for one hest the medium between his people and the void and two it is said he is the herald of the other Other gods manifesting on Earth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28439,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","user":"quelsec","date":". 05-24-2024, 02:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-26T09:24:49-07:00","id":1536304,"title":"","content":"Yes, Lovecratian mythos is fascinating, but let's not diverge too much from the topic if possible please","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-26T11:12:23-07:00","id":1536309,"title":"","content":"The harsh truth is that while the canon model for the Umbra can work, the developers should have taken lessons from D&amp;D's Planescape.<br /> <br /> 1- We have a lot of metaphysical explanations, little actual descriptions of the places the PCs are exploring and very few examples of the things and entities they'll interact with. The core book specially should have less word count on the metaphysics of the Umbra and more on describing places to explore;<br /> <br /> 2- Get rid of the Vidare. The idea is good, but it only makes things hard to explain, understand, and more importantly, to describe. At most the Vidare could apply to the Periphery, but once a group travels to the Penumbra, everyone should see the same place. Better yet would be for the three Vidare to become distinct Penumbrae;<br /> <br /> 3- Define Transition Realms. WoD's Umbra does have them, but they are ill defined, unexplained and inconsistently addressed. Take time to actually explain what is it like to be in the Middle Umbra without being in any particular Realm;<br /> <br /> 4- Astral Umbra must be redesigned almost from scratch. The place is a helluva mess to actually use on play. Take the time to define it's own Transition Realm, then look at how D&amp;D works with the Outer Planes, as they're exactly the kind of Realm found here. The place may be abstract by nature, but we need it filtered to a physical experience so we can actually explore it;<br /> <br /> 5- Make a fucking map. It isn't cheap to commission and it kinda goes against WoD's style, but that's a huge help for STs to wrap their minds around the concepts. It doesn't really matter if no map can accurately describe the Umbra, they can describe a vision of the Umbra that's good enough to start things around it.<br /> <br /> However the Umbra works, the problem is that the books devote a lot of space trying to explain metaphysics and little translating it to descriptions and rules actually useful for the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":5826,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","user":"monteparnas","date":". 05-26-2024, 05:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-17T09:43:38-07:00","id":1537563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1535582-alternate-otherworlds-structure?p=1535749#post1535749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's the idea. We can leave room for [the cosmologies of the Night Folk] if we want, but for the purposes of this thread there's no reason to limit cosmology by what they need.</div> </div> </div> </div>Room for them is provided implicitly by the fact that you need to be able to account for mages with cosmologies that align with the various Nightfolk. Shamans who see the world in a manner similar to how werewolves see the world will access Otherworlds similar to <b>Werewolf</b>'s Umbra; necromancers who see the world the same way that wraiths do will have access to the same Underworld that <b>Wraith</b> describes; and enchantresses who view reality the same way that <b>Changeling</b>'s fae do will be able to access the Dreaming described in that book. <br /> <br /> But not every shaman <i>will</i> see the world the way the Garou do; not every necromancer understands death and the dead the way wraiths do; and not every \u201cFaerie Faith\u201d mage sees the world the way changelings do. And there's no guarantee that werewolves, wraiths, and changelings even <i>exist</i> in a particular Storyteller's World of Darkness \u2014 or that if they <i>do</i> exist, that they'll bear any resemblance to the other gamelines. This cosmological model strives to be agnostic concerning the existence of nature of the other gamelines. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1535582-alternate-otherworlds-structure?p=1535749#post1535749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like this as it gives the impression that there is a lot out there and no one is even close to a complete map. I probably would have overlaps between broadly similar concepts, particularly things like the Astral realm. That doesn't mean everyone is going to the same part of that place, but it allows for conflicts in those regions. From a gameplay standpoint, it allows more interaction between mages in those regions.</div> </div> </div> </div> In this regard, I might group Otherworlds according to which Sphere is used to access them, possibly even introducing a paradigm-neutral \u201cinterstitial space\u201d for each: Mind lets you access an Astral Space, an interstitial space which contains Mind-friendly Reality Zones that provide portals to the so-called Astral Realms (and, if it exists, the Dreaming); Entropy lets you access an interstitial space where themes of death and the dead are prevalent, with Reality Zones that provide gates to various Afterlives; Correspondence lets you access \u201cvirtual space\u201d with Reality Zones that provide access to various Digital Web sites and even physical locations (with the part that links to the latter more commonly being referred to by the tech-inclined as Hyperspace), but also to Reality Zones that link to a Platonic reality where mathematical and geometric concepts have a tangible reality; Forces and Matter let you access interstitial planes containing Element-themed Reality Zones; Prime gets you to an interstitial space tied to \u201cResonance Realms\u201d which are defined by \u201cactions have consequences\u201d (among other things, Heavens and Hells would be connected here); Time lets you access a \u201cTimestream\u201d interstitial space with Reality Zones representing significant moments in time and with access to Everett Volumes; and so on. <br /> <br /> In all of these cases, I'd present the interstitial spaces as mostly empty in and of themselves, with what little definition they have coming from the Sphere used to access them, and any denizens mostly consisting of natives of the Realms that the interstitial space links to; that is, no native population. The premise for them would be \u201cit's a boring place to visit, and I wouldn't want to live there.\u201d<br /> <br /> And some or all of them may conceptually have a \u201ccenter\u201d which, if you can find it, provides easy access to all of the associated Realms: the Correspondence Point for Correspondence; Eternity for Time; an All-Mind(?) for Mind; Oblivion for Entropy; and so on. These centers aren't easy to reach, and likely will destroy you if you're not properly prepared; access to them is likely restricted to Masters, or possibly even to Archmasters. Call them Nexi (singular Nexus) when you need a collective term for them. <br /> <br /> Conversely, Paradox Realms would be \u201ccracks\u201d in these interstitial spaces, the conceptual inversion of the Nexi. They're disturbingly easy to get into, and very difficult to get out of. <br /> <br /> Finally, I'd be inclined to redefine Spirit in this cosmology, to give it a distinct role: perhaps make it less about \u201ccontacting spirits\u201d and more about \u201cthe state of being spirited\u201d \u2014 that is, a Sphere for feelings, as distinct from Mind which is a Sphere for ideas. If Werewolf-specific cosmology exists as part of this, it would specifically be tied to Rage, whereas the interstitial Spirit plane would also include regions and Realms dealing with joy, sadness, fear, disgust, and so on. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1535582-alternate-otherworlds-structure?p=1535749#post1535749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is making me picture the spirit world, in general in a more Orpheus sense, where there isn't a gauntlet between the spirit world and the physical world. Instead difficult lies in getting from there to the deeper, more specific spirit realms. That difficulty could be a barrier like a gauntlet or Orpheus' Stormwall, or it could be something else.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much what I was thinking, yes: no \u201cPenumbra\u201d per se; just insubstantial entities existing in the physical world. In particular, that's where I was suggesting that Reality Zones might contain gateways leading to appropriate Otherworlds.<br /> <br /> But it would also be true that being in an appropriate Reality Zone might also allow for Liminal Spaces (where you wander into the Liminal Space from one side, gradually lose contact with the world you left, gradually establish contact with the world of your destination, and finally emerge from the Liminal Space; more like crossing a bridge than walking through a door), or Stepping Sideways to an appropriate Otherworld, or projecting your consciousness into the Otherworld, with the access to each of these defined by the nature of the Reality Zone you're in and of the world you're trying to reach. <br /> <br /> And just like the nature of the Reality Zone determines what Otherworlds are accessible and how they're accessed, it would also determine what sorts of spirits, if any, tend to hang out in that RZ.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-18T06:23:09-07:00","id":1537608,"title":"","content":"One of the problems I have is that I always want to keep &quot;spirit stuff&quot; within the purview of the &quot;spirit powah&quot;. That is, I would like to keep all of the &quot;weird 'otherwordly' stuff&quot; within the Sphere/Domain of Spirit.<br /> <br /> I'm... Not a fan of having those being touched by other Spheres... On the other hand thou, I also don't like the idea that, once you've left the 'Material Plane', Spirit just becomes the &quot;Unified Field&quot; of Spheres, capable of doing everything out there - for which I mean, I still want a lightning to be controlled by Forces, thank you very much, even if it is technically a &quot;spiritual lightning&quot;. I particularly have a problem with the fact that, aside from the stuff that you somehow &quot;ephemerized&quot; from the Material Plane, Matter Sphere becomes useless.<br /> <br /> I'm not so fond of the idea that Spirit becomes the &quot;Sphere of emotions&quot;. That leaves Mind to be just a sphere of pure cognition, and that is... Weird. Emotions are part of the Mind, even more so than memory and cognition.<br /> <br /> I think Matter SHOULD affect the &quot;matter&quot; of the otherworlds, even if they are &quot;just&quot; 'ephemeral matter&quot;. And perhaps, even Life should affect the spirit beings directly. Spirit perhaps thus, should affect something deeper, something more... Conceptual. For instance, you could 'shapeshift' a Spirit with Life, but with Spirit 5 you change that Spirit's &quot;concept&quot;, therefore 'truly' changing it - aka, with Life the thing would suffer Pattern Bleeding, Permadox and whatnot, but with Spirit it would be a &quot;true&quot; shapeshift.<br /> <br /> Anyway, those are indeed some hard aspects to consider, and my opinion isn't set on stone on them on either way","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-18T07:09:47-07:00","id":1537613,"title":"","content":"It goes without saying that \u201cyou do you\u201d: if you don't like my suggestions, you don't have to use them. With that said: <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1535582-alternate-otherworlds-structure?p=1537608#post1537608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the problems I have is that I always want to keep &quot;spirit stuff&quot; within the purview of the &quot;spirit powah&quot;. That is, I would like to keep all of the &quot;weird 'otherwordly' stuff&quot; within the Sphere/Domain of Spirit.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be a change from how <b>Mage</b> currently does it: you don't, for example, need Spirit in order to interact with the Digital Web. I <i>could</i> see going the other way and requiring Spirit to access the Digital Web as well, though I'm not a fan of that. But: <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1535582-alternate-otherworlds-structure?p=1537608#post1537608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm... Not a fan of having those being touched by other Spheres... On the other hand thou, I also don't like the idea that, once you've left the 'Material Plane', Spirit just becomes the &quot;Unified Field&quot; of Spheres, capable of doing everything out there - for which I mean, I still want a lightning to be controlled by Forces, thank you very much, even if it is technically a &quot;spiritual lightning&quot;. I particularly have a problem with the fact that, aside from the stuff that you somehow &quot;ephemerized&quot; from the Material Plane, Matter Sphere becomes useless.</div> </div> </div> </div>That makes sense in terms of the Pattern Spheres; though you still run into problems as to issues such as \u201cwhen do you use Spirit, and when do you use Mind?\u201d I'm thinking in particular of wards, summonings, bindings, and the like: on what basis do you say, e.g., \u201cI can't use Mind to cause the spirits approaching the area to show an aversion to it and to stay away; I have to use Spirit for that\u201d? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1535582-alternate-otherworlds-structure?p=1537608#post1537608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not so fond of the idea that Spirit becomes the &quot;Sphere of emotions&quot;. That leaves Mind to be just a sphere of pure cognition, and that is... Weird. Emotions are part of the Mind, even more so than memory and cognition.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's no stranger than the fact that Matter doesn't let you manipulate air or fire; it's basically limited to the more tangible of the Elements, the solids and liquids. You need <i>two </i>Spheres, Matter <i>and </i>Forces, to address the Elements. In a similar way, my idea is to take the issue of psychological makeup and distribute it between two Spheres: a Mind Sphere that's roughly analogous to Matter, and a Spirit Sphere that's roughly analogous to Forces. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1535582-alternate-otherworlds-structure?p=1537608#post1537608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Matter SHOULD affect the &quot;matter&quot; of the otherworlds, even if they are &quot;just&quot; 'ephemeral matter&quot;. And perhaps, even Life should affect the spirit beings directly. Spirit perhaps thus, should affect something deeper, something more... Conceptual. For instance, you could 'shapeshift' a Spirit with Life, but with Spirit 5 you change that Spirit's &quot;concept&quot;, therefore 'truly' changing it - aka, with Life the thing would suffer Pattern Bleeding, Permadox and whatnot, but with Spirit it would be a &quot;true&quot; shapeshift.</div> </div> </div> </div>But should that be restricted to spirits, though? It cuts both ways: if you're using Life to affect spirits, and you use Spirit to do something \u201cdeeper\u201d, then why can't you apply the same logic to <i>people</i>? Don't they also have a \u201cdeeper, conceptual level\u201d? And if not Spirit, then what would you use to manipulate that deeper, conceptual level in humans (or animals)? Prime, maybe? <br /> <br /> But turning it around again: if you use Prime to influence people on a deeper, more conceptual level, then why don't you use Prime to influence <i>spirits</i> in the same way? <br /> <br /> Which brings me back to the notion of redefining Spirit so that it's not specifically about spirits. I went with \u201cthinking vs. feeling\u201d because it's usually easy to make that distinction, which is an advantage in gameplay; but I could also see a notion of \u201cSpirit deals with things that are spiritual\u201d, including not just animistic spirits and ghosts but also the souls of living human beings. Doing this would involve taking a closer look at what distinguishes Spirit from <i>Prime</i>, though. What makes something \u201cspiritual\u201d rather than \u201cmystical\u201d or \u201cdivine\u201d? <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-18T14:51:30-07:00","id":1537638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1535582-alternate-otherworlds-structure?p=1537613#post1537613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It goes without saying that \u201cyou do you\u201d: if you don't like my suggestions, you don't have to use them. With that said:<br /> <br /> <br /> That would be a change from how <b>Mage</b> currently does it: you don't, for example, need Spirit in order to interact with the Digital Web. I <i>could</i> see going the other way and requiring Spirit to access the Digital Web as well, though I'm not a fan of that. But:<br /> <br /> <br /> That makes sense in terms of the Pattern Spheres; though you still run into problems as to issues such as \u201cwhen do you use Spirit, and when do you use Mind?\u201d I'm thinking in particular of wards, summonings, bindings, and the like: on what basis do you say, e.g., \u201cI can't use Mind to cause the spirits approaching the area to show an aversion to it and to stay away; I have to use Spirit for that\u201d?<br /> <br /> <br /> It's no stranger than the fact that Matter doesn't let you manipulate air or fire; it's basically limited to the more tangible of the Elements, the solids and liquids. You need <i>two </i>Spheres, Matter <i>and </i>Forces, to address the Elements. In a similar way, my idea is to take the issue of psychological makeup and distribute it between two Spheres: a Mind Sphere that's roughly analogous to Matter, and a Spirit Sphere that's roughly analogous to Forces.<br /> <br /> <br /> But should that be restricted to spirits, though? It cuts both ways: if you're using Life to affect spirits, and you use Spirit to do something \u201cdeeper\u201d, then why can't you apply the same logic to <i>people</i>? Don't they also have a \u201cdeeper, conceptual level\u201d? And if not Spirit, then what would you use to manipulate that deeper, conceptual level in humans (or animals)? Prime, maybe?<br /> <br /> But turning it around again: if you use Prime to influence people on a deeper, more conceptual level, then why don't you use Prime to influence <i>spirits</i> in the same way?<br /> <br /> Which brings me back to the notion of redefining Spirit so that it's not specifically about spirits. I went with \u201cthinking vs. feeling\u201d because it's usually easy to make that distinction, which is an advantage in gameplay; but I could also see a notion of \u201cSpirit deals with things that are spiritual\u201d, including not just animistic spirits and ghosts but also the souls of living human beings. Doing this would involve taking a closer look at what distinguishes Spirit from <i>Prime</i>, though. What makes something \u201cspiritual\u201d rather than \u201cmystical\u201d or \u201cdivine\u201d?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, those are many of the same questions I have. As it is, I find it all a little fuzzy.<br /> <br /> By the way, Matter let's you manipulate air I believe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-19T06:46:19-07:00","id":1537652,"title":"","content":"Also not a fan of those distinctions. A fuel for thought non the less.<br /> Im starting to think it would be better if Spirit affected only travel between realms and affecting spirit creatures. And thats it. No affecting of the actual spiritual wold element, just spirit creatures.<br /> <br /> In effect it would only replace life but not be a dirrect copy. With that in mind you can see, touch, harm, compel, transform and bind spirits.Seems narrow but if we add that spirits with their charms can replace you any other sphere it becomes fair game. Just the matter of negotiations with said spirits and finding the useful ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-08T08:14:46-07:00","id":1538234,"title":"","content":"One idea I remember from a while back (I don't know if I saw it or made it up) was that in a default spirit world, the Spirit Sphere could replace one of the relevant Pattern spheres in a spell, but not more than that. That is, a conjunctional Life 3/Matter 2 spell could be done as a Spirit 3/Matter 2 spell or as a Life 3/Spirit 2 spell, but not as a plain Spirit 3 spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-09T12:23:04-07:00","id":1538311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1535582-alternate-otherworlds-structure?p=1538234#post1538234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One idea I remember from a while back (I don't know if I saw it or made it up) was that in a default spirit world, the Spirit Sphere could replace one of the relevant Pattern spheres in a spell, but not more than that. That is, a conjunctional Life 3/Matter 2 spell could be done as a Spirit 3/Matter 2 spell or as a Life 3/Spirit 2 spell, but not as a plain Spirit 3 spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is actually interesting. It is kind of... Well, I don't even know the word, but I honestly don't like that Spirit is the Uber-Sphere for everything outside of the Material Plane, and given that this represents a plethora of possibly infinite realms, each of which are potentially infinite, this means that Spirit alone deals with pretty much everything that exists in existence.<br /> <br /> This one is an interesting idea, but I still would want for something with a little bit more elegance for this conundrum","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-09T12:46:06-07:00","id":1538313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1535582-alternate-otherworlds-structure?p=1538234#post1538234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One idea I remember from a while back (I don't know if I saw it or made it up) was that in a default spirit world, the Spirit Sphere could replace one of the relevant Pattern spheres in a spell, but not more than that. That is, a conjunctional Life 3/Matter 2 spell could be done as a Spirit 3/Matter 2 spell or as a Life 3/Spirit 2 spell, but not as a plain Spirit 3 spell.</div> </div> </div> </div> That is actually interesting. It is kind of... Well, I don't even know the word, but I honestly don't like that Spirit is the Uber-Sphere for everything outside of the Material Plane, and given that this represents a plethora of possibly infinite realms, each of which are potentially infinite, this means that Spirit alone deals with pretty much everything that exists in existence.<br /> <br /> This one is an interesting idea, but I still would want for something with a little bit more elegance for this conundrum... Maybe something more related to Platonic ideas, some deeper level of abstraction of the things, rather than direct control of the things themselves.<br /> <br /> I gotta say, I liked the ideas from Dataweaver. I do think that Spirit should work both ways, and indeed affect things in the Material Plane at a deeper, abstract level. Just as a fleeting though, it just crossed my mind, for instance, to &quot;spiritually shift&quot; a person into a &quot;wolf&quot;, for instance. No, that person isn't shapeshifted into a wolf; for that, you would need Life. However, changing that person into a &quot;wolf&quot; in a conceptual, metaphysical sense, would mean that the person would acquire &quot;lupus-like&quot; behavior... With enough successes, the victim could even face an inexplicable urge to bark to the full moon... The victim could of course repress those strange urges, but that would be like fighting an addiction or for someone with anger issues to try to keep calm.<br /> <br /> Over time, either the concept or the material would impose itself. The victim could start to grow additional body hair, increased smell and hearing and some such.<br /> <br /> A person whose spiritual concept becomes &quot;infected&quot; by a plant-like spiritual concept could become fanatic about sun bathing constantly, develop an obsession about bees and butterflies (possibly even attracting those and other insects) and becoming much more lethargic.<br /> <br /> &quot;Infecting&quot; someone's Spirit with &quot;conceptual fire&quot; would not only turn the victim into a potential arsonist, but also make him much more energetic, with a vibrant personality.<br /> <br /> &quot;Infecting&quot; someone with water-concept would not only make the person become a bathing freak and addicted to cleaning, but could even turn a regular person into a potential Olympic champion of swimming, since that person would literally &quot;flow&quot; inside of the water, since in a deeper conceptual level besides the shadows world of the material, that person IS water.<br /> <br /> And so on. Those are just some examples, but it could work somewhat like that<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-09T15:55:31-07:00","id":1538329,"title":"","content":"Kind of like what happens when a Spirit bonds with you and you become a Fomori, but without the boosts or powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-09T17:13:38-07:00","id":1538331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1535582-alternate-otherworlds-structure?p=1538329#post1538329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kind of like what happens when a Spirit bonds with you and you become a Fomori, but without the boosts or powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes! That would be a really interesting aspect of the use of Spirit Sphere, while leaving room for the other Spheres in the vastness of the Umbra.<br /> <br /> Edit: also, I had not thought about this, but the &quot;powers&quot; COULD be a possibility - not a <i>necessity</i>, you could just give the &quot;side effects&quot; if you want to, but given enough successes and the desire, maybe some &quot;Fomori-like&quot; abilities could be feasible. That could be related to level too, so for example, a true &quot;Fomori-like&quot; &quot;supernatural&quot; would require Spirit 5, but granting a wolf smell (a &quot;mundane&quot; trait) would need just Spirit 3.<br /> <br /> In this respect, maybe we could look at Life and/or Matter as a guideline.<br /> <br /> Also, what is the name of those &quot;Fomori of Gaia&quot;? AKA, humans who are &quot;infected&quot; by spirits of Gaia, rather than spirits of the Wyrm? I forgot the name, but they exist... It would be more or less like that.<br /> <br /> Also, Avatars can have traits there are something like that. A Mage can, for instance, have the Avatar of the &quot;Great Eagle&quot; or similar, and that affects how they interact with their Avatar. So, it's not a completely alien concept either","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28035,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","user":"Magus Maximus","date":". 07-09-2024, 08:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-09T18:41:21-07:00","id":1538336,"title":"","content":"If powers are provided, make it a higher rank Effect. My concern, though, is that this is getting back into the uber-Sphere territory; so maybe it also requires Conjunctional use of whatever Sphere government the desired power. <br /> <br /> Another thing to consider is that there are spiritual traditions (deliberately lower case) that believe in such things as therianthopes: people with the body of a human but the soul/spirit of an animal. Those examples you have for how you can use Spirit to change someone's nature can also work the other way around: someone with a fiery temper might register as having Fire in his soul to someone with Spirit 1, for instance. <br /> <br /> Maybe put the Avatar Essence under the purview of Spirit? A case could be made that the Four Temperaments model of personality types correlates roughly with the Avatar Essences, and that a Sleeping Avatar's Essence manifests in the Sleeper's temperament. Both Mind and Spirit inform a person's emotional make-up, though in different ways. \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> And different Focuses will interpret this differently; so don't feel too locked in to a particular view of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-15T07:36:29-07:00","id":1538603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1535582-alternate-otherworlds-structure?p=1538234#post1538234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One idea I remember from a while back (I don't know if I saw it or made it up) was that in a default spirit world, the Spirit Sphere could replace one of the relevant Pattern spheres in a spell, but not more than that. That is, a conjunctional Life 3/Matter 2 spell could be done as a Spirit 3/Matter 2 spell or as a Life 3/Spirit 2 spell, but not as a plain Spirit 3 spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>Going over my lists for another thread I realized that M20 has an official statement on this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>M20, page 485</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Life and Matter don\u2019t work on Umbral creatures or objects unless those targets originated in the material world. Life would work on a Black Suit, for example, but not on a stag spirit.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-15T09:34:17-07:00","id":1538609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l